    "description": "Objective\n\nDecide how (or whether) to give Player, Referrer, Operator, and Partner each their own Console navigation tab, since native object tabs are capped at one per object and an App Page workaround breaks standard Console behavior.\n\nImplementation Requirements\n\nDocument findings from the App Page approach (functional, but breaks Console behavior) and the native tab approach (one tab per object max)\n\nEvaluate whether a custom LWC navigation item is worth the build cost vs. accepting the current single-tab-per-object-type compromise\n\nBring a recommendation back for a go/no-go decision\n\nAcceptance Criteria\n\nWritten recommendation with effort estimate for the chosen path\n\nOut of Scope\n\nBuilding the custom LWC itself (would be a separate ticket if approved)\n\nAdditional Notes\n\nExplicitly deferred as a non-blocker for the 7/8 demo.\n\n\\----------------------------------------\n\nEstimate: XXS · \\~1-2h (writeup only) · Dependencies: None · Ticket POC-23 (approved 2026-07-07)\n\nSource: Raised during internal build session, 2026-07-07.",
